# Gitignored files Codex and Claude Code copy from the main checkout into new
# managed worktrees. `.gitignore` syntax; a path is copied only when it matches
# a pattern here *and* is gitignored, so tracked files are never duplicated:
# https://code.claude.com/docs/en/worktrees#copy-gitignored-files-into-worktrees
# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/environments/git-worktrees#copy-ignored-local-files-into-managed-worktrees
# See docs/worktrees.md.

# Optional MCP credentials `vp run agents:sync` reads. Anchored: only the repo
# root's copy is meant.
/.agents/local.json

# The MCP servers Claude Code loads for this project, generated by
# `vp run agents:sync`. Syncing in the worktree is not a substitute: Claude Code
# reads MCP configuration once, at session start, before a fresh worktree has
# been installed. The copy comes from the main checkout, which therefore has to
# have been synced; `scripts/check-claude-mcp.ts` says so at SessionStart.
/.mcp.json

# Codex's project configuration, generated by the same sync.
/.codex/config.toml

# Local env overrides. The committed `.env.schema` files resolve credentials
# from 1Password, but a `.env` or `.env.local` still wins over the schema, so a
# checkout that points a package somewhere else on purpose carries that into its
# worktrees. `*` does not cross `/`, so these match exactly one level under
# `apps/` and `packages/`. `.dev.vars` is not copied: varlock injects Cloudflare
# env itself and refuses to build while one exists.
apps/*/.env
apps/*/.env.local
packages/*/.env
packages/*/.env.local

# Deliberately not here: deployment credentials (`.dev.vars.*`, `.env.prod`
# overrides and the like) and local databases such as `data.db` and
# `data.duckdb`. A worktree needs neither to run, and copying a database gives
# two checkouts diverging copies of state that looks shared.
